#: ../../source/model-zoo/models/keenkt.md:12 084b354ffc214d52b5917d9308acb168
msgid "原文摘要"
msgstr "Abstract"

#: ../../source/model-zoo/models/keenkt.md:14 32cf5b20a3fd439da1675ff8437e152e
msgid ""
"Knowledge Tracing (KT) aims to dynamically model a student’s mastery of "
"knowledge concepts based on their historical learning interactions. Most "
"current methods rely on single-point estimates, which cannot distinguish "
"true ability from outburst or carelessness, creating ambiguity in judging"
" mastery. To address this issue, we propose a Knowledge Mastery-State "
"Disambiguation for Knowledge Tracing model (KeenKT), which represents a "
"student’s knowledge state at each interaction using a Normal-Inverse-"
"Gaussian (NIG) distribution, thereby capturing the fluctuations in "
"student learning behaviors. Furthermore, we design an NIG-distance-based "
"attention mechanism to model the dynamic evolution of the knowledge "
"state. In addition, we introduce a diffusion-based denoising "
"reconstruction loss and a distributional contrastive learning loss to "
"enhance the model’s robustness. Extensive experiments on six public "
"datasets demonstrate that KeenKT outperforms state-of-the-art KT models "
"in terms of prediction accuracy and sensitivity to behavioral "
"fluctuations. The proposed method yields the maximum AUC improvement of "
"5.85% and the maximum ACC improvement of 6.89%."
msgstr ""
"Knowledge Tracing (KT) aims to dynamically model a student’s mastery of "
"knowledge concepts based on their historical learning interactions. Most "
"current methods rely on single-point estimates, which cannot distinguish "
"true ability from outburst or carelessness, creating ambiguity in judging"
" mastery. To address this issue, we propose a Knowledge Mastery-State "
"Disambiguation for Knowledge Tracing model (KeenKT), which represents a "
"student’s knowledge state at each interaction using a Normal-Inverse-"
"Gaussian (NIG) distribution, thereby capturing the fluctuations in "
"student learning behaviors. Furthermore, we design an NIG-distance-based "
"attention mechanism to model the dynamic evolution of the knowledge "
"state. In addition, we introduce a diffusion-based denoising "
"reconstruction loss and a distributional contrastive learning loss to "
"enhance the model’s robustness. Extensive experiments on six public "
"datasets demonstrate that KeenKT outperforms state-of-the-art KT models "
"in terms of prediction accuracy and sensitivity to behavioral "
"fluctuations. The proposed method yields the maximum AUC improvement of "
"5.85% and the maximum ACC improvement of 6.89%."

